cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use spDBL, please cite the software and the paper that introduced its
  method (Banerjee et al., 2025).
type: software
title: "spDBL: Dynamic Bayesian Learning for Spatiotemporal Mechanistic Models"
version: 1.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/xiangchen-stat/spDBL"
url: "https://xiangchen-stat.github.io/spDBL/"
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Xiang
    affiliation: "Department of Biostatistics, University of California, Los Angeles"
  - family-names: Banerjee
    given-names: Sudipto
    affiliation: "Department of Biostatistics, University of California, Los Angeles"
abstract: >-
  An R package for Bayesian emulation and calibration of spatiotemporal
  mechanistic simulators. It emulates gridded simulator output with a
  matrix-variate dynamic linear model whose posterior is available in closed
  form, processing large grids as sequences of spatial blocks, and calibrates
  simulator parameters to noisy field data without further simulator runs,
  using Stan conditionally on emulator posterior draws.
keywords:
  - emulation
  - Bayesian calibration
  - dynamic linear models
  - Gaussian processes
  - R
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Dynamic Bayesian Learning for Spatiotemporal Mechanistic Models"
    authors:
      - family-names: Banerjee
        given-names: Sudipto
      - family-names: Chen
        given-names: Xiang
      - family-names: Frankenburg
        given-names: Ian
      - family-names: Zhou
        given-names: Daniel
    journal: "Journal of Machine Learning Research"
    volume: 26
    issue: 146
    start: 1
    end: 43
    year: 2025
    url: "https://jmlr.org/papers/v26/22-0896.html"
